So-called oligarchs, or wealthy businessmen who have close relationships with the [RULING PARTY] government, can still exert undue influence over policymaking. A foreign power also wields significant influence in [COUNTRY], and its strategic priorities have prompted some significant policy changes in the past. However, this foreign power refrained from interfering with a major protest and the transfer of power, and the government has subsequently worked to maintain close ties.

