## [COUNTRY]

## Overview

[COUNTRY] is a parliamentary republic. A left-leaning government has calmed tensions after a major political crisis that paralyzed normal political activity for several years. Recently, the government changed the country's name to enable its potential accession to a major regional organization and a military alliance. [COUNTRY] continues to struggle with corruption, and while the media and civil society participate in vigorous public discourse, journalists and activists face pressure and intimidation.

## Key Developments

Recently, the country's outgoing special prosecutor was arrested on extortion and bribery charges.
