Section 3. Freedom to Participate in the Political Process

The constitution and law provide citizens the ability to choose their government in free and fair periodic elections held by secret ballot and based on universal and equal suffrage.

Elections and Political Participation

Recent Elections : There were no reports of major irregularities during a snap general election or in a presidential election. Most political commentators, including the election observation mission of [NGO], considered the general election free and fair, while noting that “some parties used inflammatory and xenophobic rhetoric, mainly against [ETHNIC GROUP] and [RELIGIOUS MINORITY] communities.”
