[NGO] reported numerous cases of controlled voting and organizational violations, that “infringe significantly voter rights and could be assessed as an indicator of deliberate interference with the electoral process” during two local election rounds.
The prosecution service reported prosecuting [NUMBER] vote-buying cases after elections; as of that time the court passed sentence in [NUMBER] of them. The [CITY] court gave a [NUMBER]-year suspended sentence and a fine to an individual for offering money to persons to vote for them as a candidate in local elections.
