## C Functioning of Government

Power remains generally centralized in the executive branch, which dominates the parliament and all other branches of government. Recent constitutional reforms introduced some measures to reduce centralization, but these reforms were in effect overridden by the [RULING PARTY]'s victory in that year's severely flawed elections.
Foreign donors have significant influence on policymaking, specifically as it relates to economic policy and public-sector reform. Business elites connected to the [RULING PARTY] have a strong impact on government decisions, particularly on those related to foreign investment in key sectors.

